{title: Swing Low, Sweet Chariot}
{artist: Wallace Willis (attributed)}
{key: D}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: 76}
{meta: public_domain African-American spiritual attributed to Wallace Willis, composed before 1862; published by the Fisk Jubilee Singers in 1872.}
{meta: source Jubilee Songs as Sung by the Jubilee Singers of Fisk University, 1872.}
{meta: arrangement Original chord arrangement for Fretlight}

{start_of_chorus}
[D]Swing low, sweet [G]chari[D]ot,
Coming for to carry me [A]home,[A]
[D]Swing low, sweet [G]chari[D]ot,
Coming for to [A]carry me [D]home.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse}
I [D]looked over Jordan, and [G]what did I [D]see,
Coming for to carry me [A]home?[A]
A [D]band of angels [G]coming after [D]me,
Coming for to [A]carry me [D]home.
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}
